    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nThis issue has been haunting my config for so long, and I finally did a bisect search to find the culprit.\n\nWhen using `vim.o.selection = 'exclusive'`, using the ci( places the cursor outside the brackets on the right side. \n\n- This happens with all 3 bracket types `([{` and all 3 quote types `` '\"` ``\n- Operators affected seem to be c and v\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n```lua\nlocal path_package = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site'\nlocal mini_path = path_package .. '/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(mini_path) then\n  vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n  local clone_cmd = {\n    'git', 'clone', '--filter=blob:none',\n    'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path\n  }\n  vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\n  vim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim | helptags ALL')\n  vim.cmd('echo \"Installed `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nend\n\nrequire('mini.ai').setup()\n\nvim.o.selection = 'exclusive'\n```\n\n3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim`.\n4. Paste the following text into the buffer and follow the instructions:\n\n```\nplace cursor anywhere in one of the below lines, except on the closing pair.\ntype ci or vi and then either the closing or opening bracket\n(periods are just added to show that you can be wherever in the line)\n\n........().........\n........[].........\n........{}.........\n........\"\".........\n........''.........\n........``.........\n```\n",
